  "articleBody": "Building a brand-new bathroom requires trade coordination that goes far beyond simple surface remodeling. Here is how to know when a professional contractor is essential.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\n- The layout sits far from existing plumbing stacks: Running long horizontal drain lines requires calculating drop per foot and ensuring clean vent penetration through the roof.\n- The new bath requires opening a concrete slab or subfloor: Cutting concrete foundations or modifying floor joists for shower traps demands proper tools and structural knowledge.\n- Adding multiple electrical circuits: Code requires dedicated GFCI protection, exhaust fan circuits, and safe lighting clearances around bathtubs and showers.\n- Waterproofing custom walk-in showers: Zero-threshold or custom-tiled walk-in showers demand professional water barriers, proper pre-slopes, and careful curb construction.\n- Managing multiple trade permits and inspections: Coordinating separate plumbing, electrical, and building inspections ensures your new addition is legal and safe.\n\nWhat to Do Next\nIf your home needs a new bathroom framed, wired, plumbed, and finished with precision tile work, hiring a hands-on general contractor keeps your project on track.\n\nContact Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC by calling 303-505-0866 to discuss your bathroom addition project today.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
